# sentence_id = 2
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = May grace and peace be multiplied to you in the knowledge of God and of Jesus our Lord, seeing that his divine power has granted us all things pertaining to life and godliness, through the knowledge of him who called us by his own glory and excellence, through which he has granted us his precious and very great promises, so that through these you may become partakers of the divine nature, having escaped the corruption that is in the world because of desire.
# literal_translation = Grace to you and peace may it be multiplied in [the] knowledge of God and of Jesus our Lord, as all things to us of his divine power the things toward life and godliness having granted, through the knowledge of the [one] having called us through glory and excellence, through which the precious and very great to us promises he has granted, so that through these you may become of divine nature partakers, having escaped from the in the world in desire corruption.
