# sentence_id = 20
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = For if God did not spare the angels who sinned, but cast them into Tartarus, delivering them to chains of nether gloom to be kept for judgment; and did not spare the ancient world, but preserved Noah, a herald of righteousness, with seven others, when he brought a flood upon a world of ungodly people; and condemned to destruction the cities of Sodom and Gomorrah, reducing them to ashes, having made them an example to those who would afterward live ungodly lives; and rescued righteous Lot, worn down by the licentious conduct of the lawless — for that righteous man, dwelling among them, tormented his righteous soul day by day by what he saw and heard of their lawless deeds — then the Lord knows how to rescue the godly out of trial, and to keep the unrighteous under punishment for the day of judgment, especially those who go after the flesh in the desire of defilement and despise lordship.
# literal_translation = For if God did not spare angels having sinned, but having cast them into Tartarus with chains of nether-gloom delivered [them], being kept for judgment; and [if] he did not spare the ancient world, but guarded Noah eighth, a herald of righteousness, having brought a flood upon a world of ungodly [people]; and [if] having turned to ashes [the] cities of Sodom and Gomorrah he condemned [them] with destruction, having set [them as] an example of things about to be to ungodly [people]; and rescued righteous Lot, being worn down by the conduct in licentiousness of the lawless ones — for by seeing and by hearing that righteous [man], dwelling among them, day by day was tormenting [his] righteous soul with [their] lawless deeds — [then] the Lord knows [how] to rescue [the] godly out of trial, but to keep [the] unrighteous, being punished, for a day of judgment, and especially those going after [the] flesh in desire of defilement and despising lordship.
