# sentence_id = 23
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = Counting pleasure the revelry of the daytime to be a delight, they are stains and blemishes, reveling in their deceits while feasting together with you, having eyes full of adultery and unceasing in sin, enticing unstable souls, having a heart trained in greed, children of a curse — abandoning the straight way, they have gone astray, having followed the way of Balaam the son of Beor, who loved the wages of unrighteousness, but received a rebuke of his own transgression.
# literal_translation = Considering pleasure the luxury in the daytime [to be], spots and blemishes, reveling in their deceits, feasting together with you, having eyes full of an adulteress and unceasing of sin, enticing unstable souls, having a heart trained of greed, children of a curse — abandoning the straight way they went astray, having followed the way of Balaam of Beor, who loved a wage of unrighteousness but received a rebuke of his own transgression.
